course: dictionary
lesson: 11290
title: Slang and sounds
level: primary-5
stars: 0
explain: Slang is informal everyday talk, often used among friends. It is not always polite, so you need to know how a word feels as well as what it means. «Wuss» is slang, and it is mildly rude. People use it to tease someone who seems scared or not brave.
explain: The example sentences do not show that meaning. They show «Worcestershire is said "WUSS-ter-sher"», so wuss is only a sound inside a place name there. Context cannot tell you the slang meaning, so a dictionary has to settle it.
explain: The same letters can make different sounds in different words. Wednesday has a silent d, and Gloucester is said "GLOS-ter". When you are not sure how a word is said, listen to people who live there, or check a dictionary.
fact: Slang is informal everyday language, often used among friends.
fact: «Wuss» (slang, mildly rude) means a person seen as weak, scared or not brave.
fact: Calling someone a «wuss» teases them, and it can be unkind.
fact: Being careful or scared of real danger is often sensible, not weak.
fact: Names keep their spelling while speech shortens them, so Worcestershire is said "WUSS-ter-sher".
exercise: A friend says, «You're a wuss for not climbing the tree!» What does wuss mean? | *A person seen as weak or scared | A kind helper | A very fast runner | A type of tree
exercise: «Worcestershire is said "WUSS-ter-sher".» Why does it sound so different from its spelling? | The letters are always said exactly as they are written | Every word with ss is said like wuss | *Place names keep their spelling while speech shortens them | It is spelled that way because it is a slang word
exercise: Is it kind to call someone a wuss for being careful near real danger? | It depends on the weather | Yes, it means they are very clever | Yes, it is always a compliment | *Not really, because being careful is often sensible
test: Which description fits «wuss»? | *A person seen as weak or scared | A kind, brave hero | A loud musical instrument | A type of bread
test: In «Wednesday has a silent d», which letter is silent? | The y | The W | The a | *The d
exam: When you are not sure how a word is said, what should you do? | Skip the word forever | Guess loudly and hope for the best | Say it exactly as it is spelled every time | *Listen to local people or check a dictionary
